		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5025&amp;p=36571#p36571"><![CDATA[
It's in the CelesTrak listing of ALL TLEs, but not in the "Amateur Radio" listing yet. I don't know if it will make it since the spaceflight will only last 4 more days maximum.<br><br>I've received 8 pictures now! It's being heavily spotted on the AMSAT Status page: <a href="https://www.amsat.org/status/" class="postlink">https://www.amsat.org/status/</a>  (Yellow means they are sending pictures).<br><br>The USSF 18th Space Defense Squadron has issued object number 63427 "DRAGON Fram2" for the mission, so I have updated my "satellites.txt" file for anyone that wants to use it: <a href="https://tinyurl.com/N9KT-satellites" class="postlink">https://tinyurl.com/N9KT-satellites</a><br><br>Right now you must use AMSAT TLEs: <a href="https://www.amsat.org/tle/dailytle.txt" class="postlink">https://www.amsat.org/tle/dailytle.txt</a> unless you use the giant file of all TLEs from CelesTrak.<br><br>The flight is also in SatNogs: <a href="https://db.satnogs.org/satellite/CXJW-8959-9671-2060-9440" class="postlink">https://db.satnogs.org/satellite/CXJW-8 ... -2060-9440</a><br><br>-David, N9KT<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2972">N9KT</a> — Wed Apr 02, 2025 10:07 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
