		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5025&amp;p=36564#p36564"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>This is the first crewed polar orbit spaceflight in history and is scheduled for 3-5 days.<br><br>My satellites.txt file with Fram2Ham in it is at: <a href="https://tinyurl.com/N9KT-satellites" class="postlink">https://tinyurl.com/N9KT-satellites</a><br><br>The TLEs are already in AMSAT's dailytle.txt: <a href="https://www.amsat.org/tle/dailytle.txt" class="postlink">https://www.amsat.org/tle/dailytle.txt</a><br><br>Fram2Ham will be sending images using Robot 36 on 437.550 MHz +/- doppler.<br><br>Upload or view images at <a href="https://ariss-usa.org/ARISS_SSTV/" class="postlink">https://ariss-usa.org/ARISS_SSTV/</a> <br>A certificate is available for uploading an image.<br><br>-David, N9KT</div></blockquote><br>Very interesting,<br><br>Do you know if celestrack will add this vehicle to their list that we normally use<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Apr 01, 2025 8:32 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
